# Urbicon UI – Cursor Rules

## Framework

Svelte 5 + Tailwind CSS 4 component library monorepo using Bun workspaces.
Components use Svelte 5 runes ($props, $state, $derived, $effect) and Snippets.

For full architecture details see `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.

## Import Rules

ALWAYS import from the package root:
```svelte
import { Button, Input, Card, Dialog, Badge, Checkbox, Toggle, Menu, Combobox, Tooltip, Spinner, Avatar, Tab, Pagination, Popover, ButtonGroup, Toolbar, Alert, Toaster, toaster, Accordion, AccordionItem, Breadcrumb, Separator, Skeleton } from '@urbicon-ui/blocks';
```

NEVER import from internal paths:
```svelte
// WRONG
import Button from '@urbicon-ui/blocks/primitives/Button/Button.svelte';
import { buttonVariants } from '@urbicon-ui/blocks/primitives/Button/button.variants';
```

For i18n: wrap the app root in `<I18nProvider locale={…}>`, read via `useI18n()` / `use<Package>I18n()` hooks (call during component init), switch with `<LocaleSwitcher>`. Without a provider, reads resolve the base locale (`en`).
```ts
import { I18nProvider, useI18n } from '@urbicon-ui/i18n';
import { LocaleSwitcher } from '@urbicon-ui/blocks';
```

## Styling Rules

### USE semantic design tokens:
- `bg-surface-base`, `bg-surface-elevated`, `bg-surface-overlay`
- `text-text-primary`, `text-text-secondary`, `text-text-tertiary`
- `border-border-subtle`, `border-border-default`
- `bg-primary`, `bg-primary-subtle` (intent fills), `text-primary-text` (intent-coloured text — never bare `text-primary`, a fill tone)
- `shadow-[var(--blocks-shadow-sm)]` through `shadow-[var(--blocks-shadow-lg)]`
- `duration-[var(--blocks-duration-fast)]`, `var(--blocks-ease-confident)`
- `z-[var(--z-modal)]`, `z-[var(--z-popover)]`, `z-[var(--z-tooltip)]`

### NEVER use:
- `dark:` prefixed classes (semantic tokens handle dark mode automatically)
- Hardcoded colors like `bg-white`, `text-neutral-900`, `border-neutral-200`
- Hardcoded `z-index` values
- `focus:` (always use `focus-visible:` for keyboard-only focus rings)
- Hardcoded `cubic-bezier` or durations
- `shadow-sm` / `shadow-md` (use `shadow-[var(--blocks-shadow-sm)]`)

## Svelte 5 Rules

- Use `$props()` – NEVER `export let`
- Use `{#snippet}` / `{@render}` – NEVER `<slot>`
- Use callback props – NEVER `createEventDispatcher()`
- Native DOM events: lowercase (`onclick`, `onfocus`, `onkeydown`)
- Custom state callbacks: `on` + PascalCase (`onCheckedChange`, `onValueChange`, `onPageChange`)
- Always pass the new state value, not the raw DOM event

## Customization Escape Hatch (Presets)

When a component needs a look **outside the semantic `intent` palette** (primary/secondary/success/warning/danger/neutral) — e.g. a dark translucent overlay, a brand color, a "glass" surface:

### USE preset registration at the app root:
```svelte
<BlocksProvider
  presets={{
    Button: {
      overlay: {
        slotClasses: {
          base: 'bg-black/20 hover:bg-black/30 active:bg-black/40 text-white border-transparent'
        }
      }
    }
  }}
>
  <Button preset="overlay">Reinholen</Button>
</BlocksProvider>
```

### NEVER use inline `class` with `!` overrides to force colors:
```svelte
<!-- WRONG — defeats hover/active cascade, inconsistent, leaks into every call site -->
<Button class="bg-black/20! hover:bg-black/30! active:bg-black/40!">Reinholen</Button>
```

Define all interactive states (`hover:`, `active:`, `focus-visible:`) inside the preset.
Merge order: the library's own tv() variant styles sit below every rung you write. Cascade (conflict-resolved per Tailwind bucket, later wins): `defaults.slotClasses → defaults.overrides[match] → preset.slotClasses → preset.overrides[match] → instance slotClasses → instance class`.

### USE `overrides` for prop-conditional rules (target only a specific variant/intent/state):
```svelte
<!-- only outlined badges get a 1px border; the tv() resolver strips the variant's border-2 -->
<BlocksProvider defaults={{ Badge: { overrides: [{ variant: 'outlined', class: { base: 'border' } }] } }}>
```
Unconditional `slotClasses` cannot do this (they hit every variant). `overrides` entries are `compoundVariant`-shaped: prop conditions (`string` = equals, `string[]` = one-of) → per-slot `class`.

## Guide System (in-app help)

The `Guide` family is a bidirectional in-app help system over one headless `GuideController`:
a non-modal help panel, contextual hints, UI↔guide links, and an opt-in spotlight tour.

### Imports
```svelte
import {
  GuideProvider, GuidePanel, GuideArticle, GuideMarker, GuideMention,
  GuideHint, Guide, GuideBeacon, GuideController
} from '@urbicon-ui/blocks';
import type { GuideTour, GuideStep, GuideStepEvent, GuideEndEvent } from '@urbicon-ui/blocks';
```

### data-guide namespace
Mark any element a topic with `data-guide="<id>"` (declarative, framework-agnostic) or
`{@attach guide.target('<id>', { label, article, direction })}` (programmatic, with metadata).
One id is shared by tours, hints, markers, and mentions:
```svelte
<button data-guide="save">Save</button>             <!-- the target -->
<GuideMarker for="save" />                            <!-- UI → panel (Direction A) -->
<GuideMention for="save">Save button</GuideMention>   <!-- panel → UI highlight (Direction B) -->
```

### DO
- Mount one `GuideProvider` near the app root and one `<Guide />` (tour renderer) inside it.
- Create the `GuideController` yourself when you need programmatic control (`startTour`, `openPanel`, `hasSeen`).
- Use `GuideBeacon` as the gentle, opt-in tour entry; keep the tour itself opt-in.
- Wire `onStep` / `onComplete` / `onSkip` on the tour — that funnel is the real value of onboarding.
- Keep guide *content* (steps, articles, selectors) in the consuming app, not the library.

### DON'T
- Don't auto-start a tour on load without user intent — Guide is "helpful, not intrusive."
- Don't wrap the panel in a modal / focus-trap — it is non-modal by design (Direction B needs the app interactive behind it).
- Don't use `Math.random()` for `data-guide` ids; they are author-chosen, stable strings.

## Component Creation

When creating new components, follow the structure and patterns in `docs/ComponentStructureStandard.md`.

Every component must support `unstyled`, `slotClasses`, `class`, and `disabled` props.
Use `tailwind-variants` (`tv()`) for all variant logic.

## Commits

Follow Conventional Commits: `<type>(<scope>): <description>`
Types: feat, fix, refactor, docs, style, test, chore, build, ci, perf

